# How omdrop-owl runs AWDL on each Wi-Fi driver. One line per kernel driver,
# named as in /sys/class/net/<iface>/device/driver. A card whose driver isn't
# listed falls back to the "*" line, and only runs with /etc/omdrop/allow-untested.
# /etc/omdrop/owl-profiles, in the same format, is read before this file: try
# settings for your card there. To add your card here, see README.md, "Adding
# your card".
#
#   status     tested: works out of the box; untested: needs allow-untested
#   mode       shared: AWDL shares the AP's channel and Wi-Fi stays connected
#              (the only mode so far; cards that can't inject while associated
#              will need an "exclusive" mode that takes Wi-Fi for the window)
#   mon_mac    station: the monitor interface carries the station's MAC, and OWL
#              reads it from there; own: it keeps a MAC of its own and OWL is
#              given the station's (owl -m)
#   reconnect  yes: force a reconnect after deleting the monitor interface, for
#              drivers whose station stops receiving after that
#   mt76_pm    yes: turn mt76 runtime power management off for the window
#   notes      the rest of the line: the hardware, and what was observed
#
# driver   status    mode    mon_mac  reconnect  mt76_pm  notes
mt7925e    tested    shared  station  yes        yes      MediaTek MT7925 (Framework 13). Injects while associated, sending from the station's MAC; the station ACKs the phone's unicast. Without a reconnect, the station stops receiving 3-165 s after a monitor interface is deleted.
*          untested  shared  station  yes        no       Any other card. Needs monitor-mode injection while associated, and an AP on channel 6, 44 or 149.
